From f4a1ae9a6c3594daf7461f4e1ec35e86e799b874 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@local>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:11:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 23/38] kebab: XNU-002a-4 register UniXNU from
 PlatformBootManagerAfterConsole

ReadyToBoot is the wrong hook: EfiSignalEventReadyToBoot() is only called
inside EfiBootManagerBoot() (BmBoot.c:2012) and BmLoadOption.c:1490, i.e.
when BDS is already launching a particular option. The boot option array
has been fetched long before that, so an option added there would not be
visible to the current menu, and could even be consumed by the retry loop
that walks the remaining options after a failure.

Registration now happens in PlatformBootManagerAfterConsole(), which BDS
calls after PlatformBootManagerBeforeConsole() (the place where Internal
Storage / USB Storage / FFU Mode are registered, BootManager.c:48) and
before BdsEntry fetches BootOptions. That is the only point where the
platform list is final and the menu has not been built yet.

- Self-gating: returns immediately when no FV contains
  GUID 9B665204-... so other Mu-Silicium devices are unaffected.
- Identity check uses the FV file GUID inside the option's device path,
  not just the description string, so a same-named foreign option is never
  overwritten.
- Still appended at the END of BootOrder; the default entry is untouched.
- XnuBootEntryDxe (ReadyToBoot variant) removed from DSC/FDF.
